alwaysApply: false
---

# TypeScript quality

- Keep `strict` TypeScript; do not weaken `tsconfig` to hide errors
- Prefer explicit props interfaces colocated with components
- Shared screen union and domain types live in `src/types.ts`
- Avoid `any`; use narrow unions for screen keys and coverage states
- Do not add `useMemo`/`useCallback` by default
- Run `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` and `pnpm run build` after substantive UI changes
- Keep apostrophe-safe string quoting to protect the Vite build
